# wisp#125 P4: Warden's neutral air held on 10 frames, each captured twice in the same held frame:
# Warden a shown, then hidden by `-dev hide fighter 0`, so Wisp's silhouetteBounds(shown, hidden)
# reads Warden's native silhouette at 1920x1080 (smashcraft:docs/commands/native.md).
#! chat -dev quick hero warden
#! silhouette a warden neutral-air 1920x1080
#! cue 122-126 nair knives: effect=FanOfKnivesMissile
# a jumps in place and plays neutral air from startup through recovery; b stands apart.
100 a tap B 8
118 a tap A 2
# Held frames: startup 119 and 121, the active knives 122 to 126, recovery 128, 131 and 134.
119 a capture
121 a capture
122 a capture
123 a capture
124 a capture
125 a capture
126 a capture
128 a capture
131 a capture
134 a capture
